<div class="container">
    <div class="iiidem-programme-overview">
        <header class="iiidem-programme-overview__header">
            <span class="iiidem-programme-overview__eyebrow">About the programme</span>
            <h2 class="iiidem-programme-overview__title">Programme Overview</h2>
            <p class="iiidem-programme-overview__intro">
                The Certificate Course on Artificial Intelligence, Elections &amp; Democratic Governance is a seven-weekend,
                practitioner-oriented, live-online programme. It requires no technical background and is designed for
                professionals as well as researchers who seek to understand or engage with AI-related challenges from
                the perspectives of governance, law, communications, and democratic process.
            </p>
        </header>

        <div class="iiidem-programme-overview__body iiidem-tabs-wrapper">
            <div class="iiidem-programme-overview__tabbar" role="presentation">
                <ul class="nav iiidem-programme-tabs" id="iiidemTab" role="tablist">
                    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                        <a class="nav-link active"
                           id="iiidem-about-tab"
                           data-toggle="tab"
                           href="#about"
                           role="tab"
                           aria-controls="about"
                           aria-selected="true">
                            AI in Elections: Opportunity &amp; Risk
                        </a>
                    </li>
                    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                        <a class="nav-link"
                           id="iiidem-whatwedo-tab"
                           data-toggle="tab"
                           href="#whatwedo"
                           role="tab"
                           aria-controls="whatwedo"
                           aria-selected="false">
                            Dual Use of AI
                        </a>
                    </li>
                    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                        <a class="nav-link"
                           id="iiidem-campus-tab"
                           data-toggle="tab"
                           href="#campus"
                           role="tab"
                           aria-controls="campus"
                           aria-selected="false">
                            The Core Challenge
                        </a>
                    </li>
                    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                        <a class="nav-link"
                           id="iiidem-organogram-tab"
                           data-toggle="tab"
                           href="#organogram"
                           role="tab"
                           aria-controls="organogram"
                           aria-selected="false">
                            Why This Course Matters
                        </a>
                    </li>
                    <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
                        <a class="nav-link"
                           id="iiidem-directory-tab"
                           data-toggle="tab"
                           href="#directory"
                           role="tab"
                           aria-controls="directory"
                           aria-selected="false">
                            What the Course Equips You With
                        </a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="tab-content iiidem-programme-panel">
                <div class="tab-pane fade show active" id="about" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="iiidem-about-tab">
                    <p>
                        This course seeks to understand how election governance can be strengthened at a time when
                        AI can improve efficiency, inclusion, accessibility, and voter services, but can also decisively
                        distort the information environment at critical moments and can be quite consequential in a
                        close or polarized election contest.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="tab-pane fade" id="whatwedo" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="iiidem-whatwedo-tab">
                    <p>
                        In other words, the same AI technologies that can spread disinformation and micro-target voters
                        can also be used to:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="iiidem-programme-panel__list">
                        <li>Counter manipulation</li>
                        <li>Detect fraud in voter rolls</li>
                        <li>Protect electoral integrity</li>
                        <li>Identify unusual patterns in ballot counting before they turn into serious problems</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="tab-pane fade" id="campus" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="iiidem-campus-tab">
                    <p>
                        The core problem is that AI is entering the electoral ecosystem faster than EMBs can understand,
                        evaluate, or govern. This course exists to close that gap.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="iiidem-programme-panel__list">
                        <li>
                            Today, EMBs are expected to build internal capacity to use AI responsibly because AI appears
                            at every stage of the electoral cycle—from voter registration to political campaigning, voting,
                            and declaration of results.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            At the same time, EMBs are also expected to safeguard democratic integrity against AI-driven
                            threats across the same electoral cycle.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="tab-pane fade" id="organogram" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="iiidem-organogram-tab">
                    <p>
                        Yet many practitioners are not adequately trained either to use AI in constructive ways or to prevent
                        the harms caused by its misuse. This gap is not a future problem. It is a present-day urgency.
                        It requires trained, informed, well-networked practitioners and experts on this specific domain.
                        That is precisely what this course aims to produce.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="tab-pane fade" id="directory" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="iiidem-directory-tab">
                    <p>The course equips participants to:</p>
                    <ul class="iiidem-programme-panel__list">
                        <li>Identify and assess AI-driven threats</li>
                        <li>Develop appropriate safeguards</li>
                        <li>Design governance and regulatory responses grounded in democratic values</li>
                        <li>Draw on comparative international experience</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['theme_iiidem2/frontpage_about_tabs'], function(tabs) {
    tabs.init();
});
{{/js}}
